  "human": "Clang can't make an executable. If it's a cross-compiler, try the --enable-cross-compile flag, but only if you actually know what cross-compiling is. The C compiler test didn't pass. If you suspect configure messed up, ensure you're on the latest Git version. If that still fails, report the issue to the mailing list or the #ffmpeg IRC channel on irc.libera.chat, and be sure to include the ffbuild/config.log file so they can help fix it.",
  "ai": "Clang is unable to generate an executable file. If Clang is functioning as a cross-compiler, utilize the --enable-cross-compile option; however, proceed only if you possess a clear understanding of cross-compilation. The C compiler test has failed. Should you believe the configure script made an error, verify that you are using the most recent version from Git. If the latest version also fails, please report the problem to the mailing list or the #ffmpeg channel on irc.libera.chat. Ensure you include the 'ffbuild/config.log' file produced by configure, as this will assist in resolving the issue."
